# November 19, 2026: Jefferson County, Washington (region wa), drawn at random by tools/choose.py. The Atlas had one place
# in Washington (Wellington and the Iron Goat Trail). This batch takes the county's Victorian seaport and the coast forts
# round it: three Army posts (the 1856 Fort Townsend, and the Endicott-era Fort Worden and Fort Flagler that guarded
# Admiralty Inlet), the Point Wilson light, Port Townsend's courthouse, city hall, customs house, Carnegie library, first
# church, a stone store of 1874, the 1868 Rothschild House with its contents, the Starrett House and Eisenbeis's brick
# "castle", the ruins of the Irondale iron and steel works, and the 1931 Enchanted Valley Chalet deep in Olympic National
# Park. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py); National Register forms from NPGallery
# (text layer read) for the courthouse, city hall, Leader Building, customs house, Carnegie library, St. Paul's, Starrett
# House, Manresa Hall and the Irondale district; Washington State Parks' park pages and park histories; the Jefferson
# County Historical Society's museum and Rothschild House pages; the Department of Ecology's Irondale cleanup page; the
# National Park Service's East Fork Quinault trail page; the Peninsula Daily News, the Port Townsend Leader and the
# University of Washington's Pacific Coast Architecture Database (PCAD).
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
